! C.frr — Standalone provider of D only (no upstream, no peers)
!
! Relationships (Gao-Rexford):
!   Customers: D (10.0.6.2)
!
! In _1, the S-C link is absent. C has no provider and no peers — it is only
! connected to D. C can reach D and vice versa, but C has no path to A, B, or S.
! D is a stub and will not re-export provider routes, so C's prefix (10.255.3.1/32)
! is unreachable from the rest of the network.
!
! Local preference:
!   300 = customer-learned
!
! Export policy:
!   → customers: full table (which, in practice, is only C's own prefix)

bgp community-list standard CUSTOMER-ROUTES permit 65003:100
!
ip prefix-list OWN-PREFIX seq 5 permit 10.255.3.1/32
!
route-map FROM-CUSTOMER permit 10
 set community 65003:100
 set local-preference 300
!
route-map TO-CUSTOMER permit 10
!
router bgp __ASN__
 address-family ipv4 unicast
  neighbor 10.0.6.2 route-map FROM-CUSTOMER in
  neighbor 10.0.6.2 route-map TO-CUSTOMER out
 exit-address-family
!
